# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env holds API keys on a machine with no OS credential store, and is
# the file most likely to be committed by accident. .env.example is the
# template and IS tracked; nothing else matching .env* should be.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Your data, not the project's ─────────────────────────────────────
# Running from source puts the user data folder in the project root, so
# a normal run leaves your own chats, macros and generated files sitting
# in the working tree. None of it belongs in the repository. The app
# creates each of these folders on demand, so losing them costs nothing.
/data/
/macros/
/ai/generated/
/ai/macros/
/trees/
# Written to USER_DATA_PATH, which IS the project root when running from
# source, so this is your assistant profiles rather than a template.
# ai/profiles.py creates a default one on first launch if it is absent.
/profiles.json

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Virtual environments ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PyInstaller writes dist/ and build/; Inno Setup writes the installer
# into installer/Output/. Release binaries are attached to a GitHub
# Release, not committed.
/build/
/dist/
/installer/Output/
*.manifest

# ── Editors and OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ── Logs and scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
*.bak
*.tmp
